An engineering mindset is a systematic, iterative approach to solving complex problems. 
Designing and testing solutions to problems with real world implementations in mind. Rather than searching for a single "right" answer, it involves breaking down challenges into manageable components. Often in collaboration with others multiple solutions are designed, tested rigorously and the right one(s) are implemented. But even on existing solutions there is the never ending task of testing and updating. 
In my first year as an engineering student along with succeeding in my classes I hope to find a professor in a field of interest to gain insight into what its like to be an electronics engineer. I also want to find a research opportunity of some sort. Finally, I want to learn the basics of python and continue building my skills using Solidworks.
